Band Description

Registry of Slow Witnesses is a five-member narrative ensemble built around the principle that the same sentence can acquire a different emotional and moral weight when replayed at another speed.

Milena Vuković — gusle, spoken recitation, live narrative structure, bow-pressure phrasing.
Darnell Price — slowed playback, sparse drum machine, mono sub, Slow Witness editing.
Jelena Matić — prepared Rhodes, harmonic checkpoints, dry modal voicings.
Andre Coleman — frame drum, sparse machine-percussion replacement, silence control.
Luka Stein — bass clarinet, low acoustic air, sub-free transitions, key-noise texture.

There is no conventional frontperson hierarchy in the mix even though Milena carries the narrative. Her live voice represents the current statement; Darnell's playback turns selected earlier statements into memory; Jelena fixes the harmonic room; Andre marks physical time without filling it; Luka occupies the acoustic low-mid register only where speech leaves space. Live versions vary because different sentences can become Slow Witnesses on different nights while the core text remains unchanged.

